  "caption": "Quinn's signature move is the hip hang — weight on one leg in every queue. Then the outer hip started aching, and lying on that side at night was a no.\n\nOuter hip pain is often a gluteal tendon problem rather than simply bursitis. Compression — lying on it, crossing legs, hanging on one hip — plus sudden jumps in load can irritate it.\n\nWhat can help: cut down daily compression, sleep with a pillow between the knees, build glute strength gradually toward single-leg work, go easy on aggressive outer-hip stretches, and pace long walks and stairs for now.\n\nGet it checked if pain spreads below the knee, is mainly in the groin, is severe and constant at night, or follows a fall.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
